Z||000000||William||12-17-2000||02:12 PM||||Hey, I just found both upper and lower gauge pod covers for sale and they are factory black? I thought these parts just came in brown and gray? Did any other dash parts come in black, such as the gauge pod itself, the dash, or any on the vinyl surrounds or covers? Is the seller of the covers wrong?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||12-17-2000||02:28 PM||||Without seeing it it's hard to say for sure. I have a really dark radio suround I picked up for a spare. I'd have to say it's black. If it's supposed to be gray it's so dark it may as well be black.<P>The vynle on it is almost a dead match to the black plastic substrate it's molded on.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||12-17-2000||02:45 PM||||It may be a part that was made as a NOS replacement part.  The dash and center consoles all can be painted any color.  GM was making "extra" parts and used black plastic.(?)  I seems that when I took a nick out of my dash it was black underneath.  Painted to match, now you have to know where the nick is.  When I purchased NOS body parts they all came black.||||reg||3
Z||000003||theogre||12-17-2000||02:56 PM||||I've seen more than just this one in that color. I think it was stock in some interior versions. It could be a aftermarket part. hard to say.<P>I've got one of the 2 tone dark/light gray dashes in mine. The light color is painted on. the dark is the molded color. I think only radio surrounds, and maybe gage pods, come stock in the black. I've not seen anything else stock that dark.<P>I'm not suprised if aftermarket parts need painting. Someone around has the things for the side of the seat. Those have to be painted to match to.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||12-17-2000||07:17 PM||||Mine in my 86GT (Gray interior) are black. Never thought anything of it, since I got it that way. The ones in my 85 are dark gray, very different from the 86 ones I have. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-17-2000||10:10 PM||||My 87 coupe is the dark gray, light gray combo, never thought of the radio surround as any sort of black, just darker gray.  Never knew that the lighter was painted on either, I guess that's good since there are no nicks in it for me to determine that by  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
